## Description
The `useControlledState` hook has the purpose of unify the logic about combining the value and defaultValue behaviors of a component achieving both the logics (Controlled and [Uncontrolled component](https://reactjs.org/docs/uncontrolled-components.html#default-values)).

The hook provides a filtered value updater under the controlled mode in order to delegate responsibility of updating the value to its parent.

User can also check the mode which is working each moment and get the initial value (mount cycle) any time.

## Usage
```js
const Component = ({value, defaultValue, onClick, onReset}) => {
  const [
    innerValue, // state
    setInnerValue, // state updater
    isControlledValue, // {boolean} using controlled behavior or not
    initialValue // first inner value state
  ] = useControlledState(value, defaultValue)
  const onHandler = (handler = () => null, value) => () => {
    setInnerValue(value)
    handler(value)
  }
  return (
    <FooBar
      value={innerValue}
      onClick={onHandler(onClick, innerValue)}
      onReset={onHandler(onReset, initialValue)}
    />
  )
}
```

